    {
      "id": "board",
      "type": "Model2",
      "label": "Board object",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 640,
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": "board",
        "properties": "headline,priority,footer",
        "prop-headline": "Welcome",
        "prop-priority": 2
      },
      "metadata": {
        "comment": "Id Source left at its default (Specify explicitly). \"headline\" and \"priority\" have values typed into the Object's OWN property inputs and nothing wired over them: the runtime queues each authored parameter into the node at creation (nodescope.ts), the prop-* setter marks it dirty and scheduleStore writes it into the record in the same pass — on every mount of this page (EXP-011 §71). The editor's panel hides these ports (allowConnectionsOnly); the MCP writes them with an info notice."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "postNotice",
      "type": "SetModelProperties",
      "label": "Post notice",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 400,
      "parameters": {
        "idSource": "explicit",
        "modelId": "board",
        "properties": "headline"
      }
    }
